# Pins the runtime context window.
#
# llama3.2 declares a 131072 token context, but Ollama allocates its own
# default at load time when no num_ctx is set. Measured with probe_context.py,
# that default is about 4096 tokens on this machine: a codeword placed at the
# front of the prompt was still recalled at roughly 3950 tokens and was gone by
# 6570.
#
# Ollama discards the FRONT of an oversized prompt and reports nothing. The
# context builder assembles transcript, then slide text, then notes, so the
# transcript is always what is lost first. Left unpinned, the largest deck in
# the evaluation corpus would silently degenerate into a slide-only run while
# still being labelled as a combined run.
#
# 16384 is chosen with headroom rather than to fit exactly. The quiz call is
# the larger of the two model calls because it receives the assembled context
# plus the generated notes, giving a worst case near 6700 tokens on the largest
# deck.
#
# Build with:  ollama create llama3.2-ctx16k -f Modelfile
# Then set:    OPENAI_MODEL=llama3.2-ctx16k   in .env

FROM llama3.2
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384
